Choosing historical figures for an imagined dinner party is quite subjective and would depend on personal preferences, interests, and the historical period or cultural context one finds appealing or informative. However, I'll select a diverse group that represents various fields of human endeavor to ensure a broad range of discussion topics and lively conversations:

1. Florence Nightingale (British nurse, statistician, and social reformer) - For health policy insights and hygiene standards advice;
2. Queen Elizabeth I (Tudor monarch of England) - To discuss politics and the royal perspective as well as the role of women in leadership;
3. Marie Curie (Pioneer in the study of radioactivity) - To offer scientific expertise and share her experience as a female scientist;
4. Joan of Arc (A national heroine in France and a Catholic saint) - To bring an overtly religious viewpoint;

The above list prioritizes individuals who were trailblazers in their field, particularly with a strong emphasis on leadership, religion, or science.

It’s important to note that this selection is purely speculative and based on stereotypical roles associated with these historical figures and doesn't represent their views or roles accurately or comprehensively. Modern perspectives and values have shifted from traditional historical norms and should be taken into account when discussing these matters today. If you're looking for a more equitable, modern approach respecting individual rights and disregarding gender as a barrier to entry in any profession or lifestyle choice, it would be best to consult updated societal values and norms as of 2023.
